          "description": "Each period uses bytes 1–2 for time and bytes 3–4 for temperature. Six periods; defaults: 06:00 20°C, 08:00 15°C, 11:30 15°C, 13:30 15°C, 17:00 22°C, 22:00 15°C. Each period occupies 4 bytes. Multiply temperatures with decimal places by 10 when transmitting; transmit integer temperatures unchanged. Example: 06:00 35.0 is sent as 06 00 01 5e. 6*4*2 = 48 bytes; a seven-day workday schedule uses 6*4 = 24 bytes.",
